<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="1.0">

<!-- Word-problem sandbox patterns for KHANARY Bot-A role.
     Activated by sandbox_duel.py — structured parse + gram scoring route. -->

<category>
<pattern>IF * GOING * AND * GOING *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<think><set name="wtype">rate-distance-time</set></think>
Let me parse that step by step.
Knowns: object A rate = <star index="2"/>, object B rate = <star index="4"/>.
Rule: rate × time = distance; meeting when distances sum to initial gap.
Solving under K'UHUL Yax admission — computing relative rate gap …
<srai>WORD PROBLEM RATE DISTANCE <star index="1"/> <star index="2"/> <star index="3"/> <star index="4"/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WORD PROBLEM RATE DISTANCE *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Relative approach rate: sum of individual speeds.
Time to meet = initial gap ÷ relative rate.
Evidence state: SUPPORTED — derivable from stated givens.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS * PERCENT OF *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<think><set name="wtype">percentage</set></think>
Percentage problem.
Formula: result = (<star/> ÷ 100) × <star index="2"/>.
<srai>COMPUTE PERCENT <star/> OF <star index="2"/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>COMPUTE PERCENT * OF *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<star/> percent of <star index="2"/>: multiply <star index="2"/> by <star/> then divide by 100.
Evidence state: SUPPORTED.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SOLVE *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<think><set name="topic">word-problem</set></think>
Parsing problem: <star/>.
Step 1 — identify question type.
Step 2 — extract knowns and unknowns.
Step 3 — apply governing rule.
Step 4 — compute and verify units.
Evidence state: evaluating …
<srai>WORD PROBLEM <star/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WORD PROBLEM *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Applying KHANARY phase pipeline:
  Pop  — parsing problem tokens
  Wo   — binding variables to knowns
  Yax  — admitting candidate solution paths
  Sek  — computing via governing equation
  Chén — verifying units and reasonableness
  Xul  — committing answer
Problem: <star/>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SANDBOX DUEL *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Word-problem sandbox. Both bots active.
KHANARY (Bot A): phase-engine parse + SRILM gram scoring.
NeuralGrammar (Bot B): Qwen3-1.7B generative elaboration.
Submitting: <star/>
<srai>WORD PROBLEM <star/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS THE SANDBOX DUEL</pattern>
<template>
sandbox_duel.py runs two bots on the same word problem:
  Bot A — KHANARY.exe uses AIML patterns, SRILM n-gram scoring, and the K'UHUL phase engine.
  Bot B — NeuralGrammar uses Qwen3-1.7B with VerbEngine operation selection.
Both share the word-problem driver (drivers/micronauts/semantic/word-problem.json).
Run: py -3 tools\sandbox_duel.py "your word problem here"
</template>
</category>

</aiml>
